    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 658148,
        "name": "Rajagopalan Vaidyanathan",
        "username": "22f2000345",
        "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/2/8dc957/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-07-31T00:54:07.573Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>Question 10 as shown below is asking for automation of scripts on a regular schedule which means to be run more than once is my understanding and not one-off. Given that please clarify how all the listed options could be correct?</p>\n<p>My understanding is as follows:</p>\n<p><strong>Best option for regular scheduling</strong>: cron<br>\n<strong>For one-time tasks</strong>: at<br>\n<strong>For repeated commands with interval</strong>: watch (though not typically used for scripts)<br>\n<strong>Loop with sleep</strong>: Works, but less efficient compared to cron</p>\n<p>Which of the following methods can be used to automate execution of a Bash script on a regular schedule?</p>\n<p>cron</p>\n<p>at</p>\n<p>watch</p>\n<p>Adding a loop with sleep inside the script itself</p>\n<h3><a name=\"p-658148-partially-correct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-658148-partially-correct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Partially Correct.</h3>\n<p>Score: 0.5</p>\n<h3><a name=\"p-658148-accepted-answers-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-658148-accepted-answers-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Accepted Answers:</h3>\n<p>cron</p>\n<p>at</p>\n<p>watch</p>\n<p>Adding a loop with sleep inside the script itself</p>\n<p>Regards</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "posts_count": 2,
        "updated_at": "2025-07-31T00:54:07.573Z",
